    "created_at": "2018-02-21T14:42:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-21T14:42:31Z",
    "body": "> I get that the standard is meant to prevent a return to the bad old days, but this isn't features being implemented in incompatible ways, this is a standardized option that wil only be implemented in a minority of UAs\r\n\r\nWhat makes you say that? What if the market leader ships this and developers don't care about fallback and the market leader uses the \"but we're compliant\" as a defense for spreading their proprietary variant of HTML?\r\n\r\nClosing this since it's indeed resolved, but happy to discuss further if needed.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
