    "created_at": "2018-02-21T16:15:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-21T16:15:00Z",
    "body": "That's a good point; I was thinking about supporting some previously-existing languages natively rather than requiring them be compiled to Javascript, but the same token allows deliberate proprietary lock-in.  I still think taking a hard line in excluding legitimate languages isn't the best way to go about it, but since I don't have a good alternative, I'll give you that.\n\nThe language does present a Catch-22, though; \"we'll add support for more, but only if the majority of the market ignores what we say now\".  My recommendation would be to remove the public note, and just record that the door remains open a crack for future maintainers, whether in a comment in the document itself or somewhere else easily-found and closely-associated.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
